# opfor_training.md.backup

This sanitized description captures the Opposed Force training system without referencing campaign-specific data.

## Overview

- Tracks elapsed training time and produces a scaling factor for enemy templates.
- Uses configurable difficulty curves to adjust offensive and defensive stats.
- Integrates with spawning systems so generated enemies inherit the current scaling profile.
- Supports script overrides (for example, a `opfor_scale(time)` callback) to prototype alternate progressions.

## Extended Use Cases

- Automated combat simulations can apply the same scaling rules to entire squads.
- Designers can pin minimum and maximum multipliers in data files to control test bounds.
- Telemetry hooks record progression data for balancing without storing scenario identifiers.
